Base model
----------
The recipe fine-tunes nvidia/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b by NVIDIA
(https://huggingface.co/nvidia/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b), licensed under the OpenMDW License Agreement,
version 1.1 (https://openmdw.ai/license/1-1/). The base model's weights are not included here; obtain them from
NVIDIA's model repository under its licence. Models trained with this recipe are derivatives of that model and are
subject to its licence terms. The published Ayaz ASR v0.1 weights are released under OpenMDW-1.1
(https://huggingface.co/VeliAyaz/ayaz-asr-tr-streaming-0.6b).
This work is not endorsed or supported by NVIDIA.

Software used (not included)
----------------------------
- NVIDIA NeMo (https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/NeMo), Apache License 2.0. The training code was started from NVIDIA's
  fine-tuning guide "How to fine-tune Nemotron 3.5 ASR for your language, domain, or accent" (Hugging Face Blog, 2026).
- sherpa-onnx by k2-fsa (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx), Apache License 2.0.
  export/export_onnx.py is derived from sherpa-onnx scripts/nemo/nemotron-3.5-asr-streaming-0.6b/export_onnx.py
  (commit 99ddefaa), Copyright 2026 Julian Pscheid, Apache License 2.0; modified to read a local .nemo, to write to a
  chosen directory, to leave int8 quantisation to a separate step and to take the 'comment' metadata from --label.
- ONNX and ONNX Runtime, PyTorch, Lightning, lhotse and the other packages listed in requirements.txt, each under its
  own licence.

Datasets (downloaded by the scripts, not included)
--------------------------------------------------
- YODAS, cleaned release of OWSM v4: espnet/yodas_owsmv4 (https://huggingface.co/datasets/espnet/yodas_owsmv4),
  CC-BY-3.0. Li X, Takamichi S, Saeki T, Chen W, Shiota S, Watanabe S. "YODAS: YouTube-oriented dataset for audio and
  speech." IEEE ASRU 2023. Peng Y, et al. "OWSM v4: improving open Whisper-style speech models via data scaling and
  cleaning." arXiv:2506.00338, 2025. Labels are the videos' manually written subtitles.
- YODAS2 (espnet/yodas2, https://huggingface.co/datasets/espnet/yodas2): only the list of manually subtitled Turkish
  videos (data/tr000/text, video ids) is read; see its dataset card for licence terms.
- FLEURS: google/fleurs (https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs), CC-BY-4.0. Conneau A, et al. "FLEURS: few-shot
  learning evaluation of universal representations of speech." IEEE SLT 2022.

In-house data
-------------
Ayaz ASR v0.1 additionally used consented volunteer voice messages and the developer's own recordings. These data are
not distributed and are not part of this repository.
